A tree is a leaf, or a node with a pair of subtrees. The check on the input is deep, so a node whose subtree is not a tree is refused.
---

---
type Tree = Leaf | Node (Tree . Tree)
fn t
	match t {
		Leaf -> 0
		Node p -> 1
	}
---
Leaf => 0 fuel 1000
Node (Leaf . Leaf) => 1 fuel 1000
Node (Leaf . (Node (Leaf . Leaf))) => 1 fuel 1000
Node (Leaf . 5) => error fuel 1000
~ => error fuel 1000
